Z||000000||ounmongk||02-07-2000||06:18 PM||||Are there any substitutions for dynamat? Would something along the lines of, say, foam rubber work? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||jhogans||02-07-2000||11:32 PM||||A company called McMasters, <A HREF="http://www.mcmaster.com," TARGET=_blank>www.mcmaster.com,</A>  sells some sound damping materials.  Goto their site and do a search on damping materials.  Several people on the rec.audio.car newsgroup have used this product.  It is cheaper than Dynamat.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FIEROCIOUS||02-08-2000||12:54 AM||||Go to Home depot and buy roof membrain stuff.<BR>I realy don't remember the name but it is in the roofing department it is 1/6" thick (about the same thickness as dynamat) and has a sicky backing. They sell it buy the yard and it is super SUPER cheap! Guys in my area buy it for their low rider trucks to deaden the sound in the bed after installing huge sound systems! Works great ||||reg||1
Z||000003||jhogans||02-08-2000||04:28 PM||||If you live in the south then this stuff is hard to find.  I cannot find it anywhere and I live in Atlanta, GA.  It used mostly for icing protection.||||reg||1
